\vspace{0.5cm}

{\large\bfseries\color{LiturgicalRed} 關於本書}\qquad{\large\bfseries\color{LiturgicalBlue} About This Book}

\vspace{0.5cm}

\begin{minipage}{5.4in}
\small\color{TextGray}
$if(backcover)$
$backcover$
$else$
本書以黃長老的查經方法走遍詩篇一百五十篇——依詩篇本身的五卷結構（對應摩西五經），每卷先作整卷深讀，再逐篇給出一把鑰匙：精義一句話，加上「看見耶穌」的角度。因為詩篇的主角永遠是耶穌：詩一那棵栽在溪水旁的樹、詩二受膏的王子、詩二十二被離棄的哀號者、詩二十三的好牧人、詩一百一十右邊的主與麥基洗德等次的祭司、詩一百一十八被匠人棄掉的房角石。整卷詩篇的終局，是「凡有氣息的，都要讚美耶和華」——與整本聖經的終局，同一個方向。

A psalm-by-psalm reception of the whole Psalter in Elder Huang's method: each of the five books read as a whole, then every psalm given one key — its distilled essence, and the angle from which to see Jesus Christ. For the protagonist of all 150 psalms is always Jesus: the tree planted by streams (Ps 1), the anointed Son (Ps 2), the forsaken sufferer (Ps 22), the good shepherd (Ps 23), the priest-king (Ps 110), the rejected cornerstone (Ps 118). The Psalter ends where the whole Bible ends: ``Let everything that has breath praise the LORD.''
$endif$
\end{minipage}

